    {
      "id": "render-finalize",
      "name": "RenderFinalize",
      "category": "VirtualTexturing",
      "signature": "RenderFinalize(Graph Builder, Scene Rendering Context)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Graph Builder",
          "type": "FRDGBuilder&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Scene Rendering Context",
          "type": "ISceneRenderer*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "A Finalizer is an object that does the final work of filling the physical textures.\nThe work for all finalizers is scheduled at a specific point in the frame where we can write to the physical texture without hazards, and\nwhere the virtual texture page tables are also updated.\nThe finalizer work may be split into two parts.\nRenderFinalize() does not write to the physical texture, but can read from virtual textures. This is a phase that allows any\npage rendering which may need to sample virtual textures. Runtime virtual textures and material systems require this.\nFinalise() must write to the physical textures, but cannot sample from them.\nAll finalizers need to implement Finalize() but only ones that need to sample virtual textures need to implement RenderFinalize()."
    },
